        "text": "The term Web3 was coined by Ethereum co founder Gavin Wood in 2014 to describe a decentralized Internet based on blockchain technology. As Web3 is still a nascent iteration of the future Web, there are different opinions on what it should be, but generally Web3 is envisioned as decentralized, open, and places the users at the Center. If web 1.0 is the read only web and web 2.0 is the read and write web, then web 3 is the read, write and own Web. A core vision of web 3.0 is to counter the weaknesses of web 2.0, which saw a handful of giant tech platforms dominating digital lives globally. Internet tech giants were able to distribute, censor, and monetize the data and content that everyone else was publishing on the Internet. They often also created barriers to entry so that other platforms and individuals would not threaten any monopolistic strongholds. They may have.",
